a:T1f9d,EUNHAE CHO | RESOURCE LINK DIRECTORY
Special Education · Applied Linguistics · Applied Behavior Analysis
Links reviewed November 7, 2026

Behavior Analyst Certification Board
Certification & ethics
The certification body for behavior analysts and technicians. Consult official handbooks, ethics codes, eligibility information, and ongoing certification requirements.
https://www.bacb.com/

Association for Behavior Analysis International
Behavior analysis
Connects the behavior analysis community through research, conferences, journals, special interest groups, and opportunities for professional learning.
https://www.abainternational.org/

Iowa Association for Behavior Analysis
Behavior analysis · Iowa
Iowa’s ABAI affiliated chapter advances behavior analysis through education, research, dissemination, and professional connections across the state.
https://www.iowaaba.com/index.html

Council for Exceptional Children
Special & inclusive education
A professional community supporting special education through research, professional standards, advocacy, publications, and learning opportunities for educators.
https://exceptionalchildren.org/

Division for Learning Disabilities
Special & inclusive education
A CEC division connecting learning disabilities research with effective teaching, professional collaboration, and resources for equitable educational opportunities.
https://teachingld.org/

Division for Early Childhood
Early childhood & families
Supports early intervention and early childhood special education through recommended practices, personnel preparation resources, publications, and professional learning.
https://www.dec-sped.org/

Association for Positive Behavior Support
Behavior analysis
Brings together people using positive behavior support to improve quality of life across schools, homes, workplaces, and community settings.
https://apbs.org/

American Educational Research Association
Educational research
Supports educational inquiry and the use of research through scholarly publications, conferences, professional development, and research communities.
https://www.aera.net/

AERA Special and Inclusive Education Research SIG
Special & inclusive education
A research community examining the education of people with disabilities, including access, equity, educational outcomes, and research methods.
https://www.aera.net/SIG113/Special-and-Inclusive-Education-Research-SIG-113

AERA Second Language Research SIG
Language & literacy
Connects scholars studying second language learning and teaching across research traditions, educational settings, and policy questions.
https://www.aera.net/SIG108-Second-Language-Research-SIG-108

American Association for Applied Linguistics
Language & literacy
An interdisciplinary community studying language in education and society, with scholarly exchange, mentoring, and professional development for applied linguists.
https://www.aaal.org/

TESOL International Association
Language & literacy
Supports English language teaching through professional learning, research, advocacy, and resources for educators working across multilingual educational contexts.
https://www.tesol.org/

ACTFL
Language & literacy
Offers language education research, proficiency guidance, classroom resources, and professional learning to advance multilingual and multicultural education.
https://www.actfl.org/

International Literacy Association
Language & literacy
Connects literacy research and classroom practice through professional learning, publications, and standards supporting reading and writing instruction.
https://www.literacyworldwide.org/

American Association of Colleges for Teacher Education
Teacher education
Advances educator preparation through research, policy advocacy, professional practice, and collaboration among colleges, universities, and teacher educators.
https://aacte.org/

American Speech-Language-Hearing Association
Communication & inclusion
A professional, scientific, and credentialing association offering research and resources on communication, language, hearing, and related professional practice.
https://www.asha.org/

Behavior Analyst Certification Board
Official information about individual BCBA certification, including eligibility, maintenance requirements, professional responsibilities, and the current handbook.
https://www.bacb.com/bcba/

ABAI Accreditation Board
Standards, application information, and listings for accredited academic programs in behavior analysis. Accreditation applies to educational programs.
https://accreditation.abainternational.org/welcome.aspx

Center for Disabilities and Development
University of Iowa information about disability services, appointment requests, provider referrals, family resources, and community supports.
https://uihc.org/childrens/services/center-disabilities-and-development

Iowa Family Support Network
Statewide information and referral resources connecting expecting families, families with young children, and professionals with Iowa services.
https://www.iafamilysupportnetwork.org/

Iowa Reading Research Center
University of Iowa · Literacy
University of Iowa research, professional learning, and practical literacy tools, including caregiver resources and guidance for supporting students with reading difficulties.
https://irrc.education.uiowa.edu/

University of Iowa Disability Resource Library
University of Iowa · Disability resources
Books, training materials, and reference support on disabilities, education, and assistive technology through the Center for Disabilities and Development.
https://uihc.org/childrens/locations/center-disabilities-and-development/disability-resource-library

Iowa Compass
University of Iowa · Community connections
A statewide information and referral service connecting people with disabilities and their families to community services, supports, and assistive technology resources.
https://www.iowacompass.org/

Iowa Department of Education · Special Education
Iowa · Family and school partnership
Official Iowa guidance on family participation in special education, individualized education programs, procedural safeguards, and related parent resources.
https://educate.iowa.gov/pk-12/special-education/parent-information

Grant Wood Area Education Agency
Eastern Iowa · School support
Regional special education resources and support for school teams, including instructional guidance, evaluation information, and links to procedures and forms.
https://www.gwaea.org/educators/special-education/

ASK Resource Center
Iowa · Family support
Iowa’s parent training and information center offers family-centered special education information, learning opportunities, and support for navigating educational services.
https://www.askresource.org/

Iowa City School District · Special Education
Iowa City · Local schools
Local information on special education services, accessing support, educational transitions, and resources for families and school communities.
https://www.iowacityschools.org/our-district/departments/special-education

IRIS Center
Vanderbilt University · Educator learning
Vanderbilt University modules, case studies, and classroom activities connect evidence-based instructional and behavioral practices with educator preparation and professional learning.
https://iris.peabody.vanderbilt.edu/

CAST Universal Design for Learning
Accessible instruction · UDL
Universal Design for Learning guidelines and downloadable planning tools support engagement, representation, and action and expression across diverse learners.
https://udlguidelines.cast.org/more/downloads/

Autism Focused Intervention Resources & Modules
UNC · Autism practices
UNC modules and downloadable tools guide the planning, use, and monitoring of evidence-based practices for learners on the autism spectrum.
https://afirm.fpg.unc.edu/

This directory offers external resources; inclusion does not imply membership, endorsement, or a service relationship. External materials remain on their publishers’ websites. Retain attribution and follow each resource’s reuse terms.
